<section id="signal-guide" class="signal-guide" aria-labelledby="signal-guide-title">
  <header class="signal-heading">
    <p class="signal-label">ILLUSTRATIVE SIGNALS / NOT REAL MEASUREMENTS</p>
    <h3 id="signal-guide-title">What readings can tell us</h3>
    <p>
      These invented examples explain the proposed interpretation of readings. They are not real measurements or
      validated detection thresholds.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="signal-examples">
    <figure>
      <span class="chart-axis-label">Relative power</span>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 320 136" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path class="signal-axis" d="M12 120H308"></path>
        <path
          class="signal-fill"
          d="M12 108L30 108L42 45L57 31L69 50L81 35L95 53L106 38L120 40L132 105L168 105L181 42L195 36L208 57L221 33L235 54L248 38L265 50L278 39L308 43V120H12Z"
        ></path>
        <path
          class="signal-trace"
          d="M12 108L30 108L42 45L57 31L69 50L81 35L95 53L106 38L120 40L132 105L168 105L181 42L195 36L208 57L221 33L235 54L248 38L265 50L278 39L308 43"
        ></path>
      </svg>
      <span class="chart-axis-label chart-time">Time →</span>
      <figcaption>
        <h4>A dip can be a pause</h4>
        <p>
          A brief low section is followed by renewed activity. A short drop must not be treated as a finished cycle.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <span class="chart-axis-label">Relative power</span>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 320 136" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path class="signal-axis" d="M12 120H308"></path>
        <path
          class="signal-fill"
          d="M12 108L30 108L42 43L58 32L74 52L88 37L102 49L116 29L130 45L145 34L160 44L182 107L218 106L250 107L278 106L308 107V120H12Z"
        ></path>
        <path
          class="signal-trace"
          d="M12 108L30 108L42 43L58 32L74 52L88 37L102 49L116 29L130 45L145 34L160 44L182 107L218 106L250 107L278 106L308 107"
        ></path>
      </svg>
      <span class="chart-axis-label chart-time">Time →</span>
      <figcaption>
        <h4>Low power is not availability</h4>
        <p>
          Activity settles into a low line. A low reading alone confirms neither a finished cycle nor an empty drum.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <span class="chart-axis-label">Relative power</span>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 320 136" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path class="signal-axis" d="M12 120H308"></path>
        <rect class="signal-gap" x="174" y="16" width="134" height="104"></rect>
        <path class="gap-boundary" d="M174 16V120"></path>
        <path class="signal-fill" d="M12 108L30 108L42 45L57 31L69 50L81 35L95 53L106 38L120 40L135 29L151 46V120H12Z"
        ></path>
        <path class="signal-trace" d="M12 108L30 108L42 45L57 31L69 50L81 35L95 53L106 38L120 40L135 29L151 46"></path>
        <circle class="last-reading" cx="151" cy="46" r="4"></circle>
      </svg>
      <span class="chart-axis-label chart-time">Time →</span>
      <figcaption>
        <h4>No fresh readings, no known state</h4>
        <p>The trace stops and leaves a gap. When readings are missing or stale, the current state is unknown.</p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="collection-guide">
    <h4 class="collection-title">Proposed collection flow</h4>
    <ol class="collection-flow">
      <li>
        <strong>Cycle end reported or estimated</strong>
        <p>From a supported API, or meter-based rules that still need validation.</p>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Awaiting collection</strong>
        <p>A finished programme does not confirm that the drum is empty.</p>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </li>
      <li class="resident-step">
        <span class="confirmation-label">QR confirmation</span>
        <strong>Resident confirms collection</strong>
        <p>The resident uses the machine's QR page to confirm collection.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="collection-note">
      The app would then show availability according to resident confirmation, not a sensor measurement. QR labels do
      not detect doors or an empty drum.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

